A||||5||Gomez||need help with rocker arms please!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||Gomez||08-18-2001||03:44 PM||||I need to know the micrometer measurments for the valve lash? Can anyone help me here. Everywhere I read, says 3/4-1.5 turns but the mechanic who is working on wants exact micrometer measurments. says it will be quicker??? Anyone know what he is talking about? we are supposed to finish the car up today.<BR>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||AkursedX||08-18-2001||04:53 PM||||Well, good luck finding these measurements.  But all I did when setting my valve lash wash went 3/4 of a turn past tight.  I have read anywhere from 1/2- 1-1/2 turns, but I don't think there is any real exact science on this.  But maybe I'm wrong.  <P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||08-18-2001||07:29 PM||||I'm not sure what your mech is looking for here. Is he trying to set lash with a feeler gage? or does he want torque settings for micrometer type torque wrench. You can't use any set torque. I sure don't know what he would use a feeler gage for if that is what he is refering to by 'micrometer setting'. 1/2 to 1 1/2 turns after 0 lash. Just did a long search and this is the concensus. I'm sure you are aware these are hyd lifters?<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||8Ball||08-19-2001||01:24 AM||||Me either to be honest.<BR>But whatever he wanted he found it. Almost done with my engine work but she is sounding prettygood  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||08-19-2001||08:47 AM||||Your mechanic may be confusing the iron head 2.8 with the aluminum head version.  On the aluminum heads you just torque the rockers to 18 ft-lbs.  I wish ours were so easy.  <BR>My Haynes and my GM 60 Degree V-6 Handbook both say 1.5 turns past zero lash, but zero lash seems to be subjective to me.  Is it no play or no turning of the pushrod?  The rod will still spin for a while if you lube it prior to install.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||08-19-2001||09:40 AM||||I think he is referring to a dial indicator. You need to set the lifter preload with a dial indicator to .030". Measure the amount of turns it took to get that .030" lifter preload and just turn the others the same amount in the correct order.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
